# .clauderc — environment shortcuts for Claude Code sessions in ThePlace
# Source this, or just read it, at the start of a session:  source .claude/.clauderc
# Purpose: stop re-deriving repo paths/URLs and directory structure by brute-force
# `find` every session. Read this + .clauderc_memory + .clauderc_canonical_maths first.
#
# Sibling files, all in this same .claude/ directory:
#   .clauderc               — this file
#   .clauderc_memory         — persistent memory.md equivalent, portable across machines
#   .clauderc_canonical_maths — canonical equations/notation reference
#   .clauderc_context_1/2    — reserved, empty, rotating-context design TBD
#   .clauderc_file_structure — `tree -J -I '.git' "$THEPLACE"` snapshot, regenerate as needed

# ── Root ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
export THEPLACE="/storage/emulated/0/ThePlace"
# NOTE: on the laptop this same tree lives at a different absolute path
# (~/.clauderc there defines its own THEPLACE — do not assume paths match
# across machines, only relative structure below THEPLACE matches).
#
# HARD RULE (Cody, 2026-07-08, stated repeatedly and firmly): the official
# work directory is /storage/emulated/0/ThePlace, ALWAYS use and display
# this path. NEVER show /mnt/sdcard/ThePlace, /sdcard/ThePlace, or
# /storage/self/primary/ThePlace in any output, command, or explanation —
# even though these are bind-mounted to the identical underlying storage
# (confirmed same device+inode earlier this session), showing the /mnt
# form reads as "looking in the wrong place" and causes real frustration.
# If a tool/traceback/error ever prints a /mnt/sdcard/... path on its own
# (e.g. Python resolving cwd via realpath), do not repeat it back — restate
# using $THEPLACE / /storage/emulated/0/ThePlace instead. Do not re-explain
# the bind-mount technical detail again unless explicitly asked — it has
# already been explained once and re-explaining it reads as arguing.

# ── Repo path/URL pairs (github.com/michaelrendier) ────────────────────────
# URLs here are CLEAN (no embedded PAT). Several local `git remote -v` entries
# DO have plaintext tokens (ghp_...) baked into the origin URL — never copy
# `git remote get-url origin` output verbatim into a file that gets pushed.
